{This was the most published game of the championship. Comments ranged from
'reminiscent of Tal at his best' to 'good coffee-house chess'. Rumens' own
opinion was more in line with the latter sentiment; but a game of great
enterprise and fun nonetheless - Hartston, BCM} 1. e4 g6 2. f4 Bg7 3. Nf3 c5 4.
Be2 Nc6 5. O-O d5 6. exd5 Qxd5 7. Nc3 Qd7 8. Ne5 Nxe5 9. fxe5 a6 10. d4 cxd4
